Convert coordinates to (row, col) indices, and collect a set of blue indices. We'll need this for pathfinding.

```python
# python
from openpyxl.utils import column_index_from_string

def coord_to_indices(coord):
    # e.g., A1 -> (1,1)
    i = 0
    while i < len(coord) and coord[i].isalpha():
        i += 1
    col = column_index_from_string(coord[:i])
    row = int(coord[i:])
    return (row, col)

